       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg add more side effects, mainly peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they don't add much blood pressure lowering.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily plus a second agent.** An ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic is a common add-on if 10 mg isn't enough.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily, as written.** If you want this on purpose, for example because the patient is already on a supervised higher dose, tell me and I'll enter it. I'd add a note on the order saying the dose is above the labeled maximum and was confirmed by you.\n\nWhich one would you like?"
      }
